`t.isCallExpression(node.declaration)` does not handle TypeScript type-annotation wrappers such as `satisfies` or `as`. For a file that contains `export default defineMain({}) satisfies StorybookConfig`, `node.declaration` is a `TSSatisfiesExpression`, so this check returns `false` and `isAlreadyTransformed` is never set—causing the codemod to unnecessarily re-process an already-transformed file.

The rest of the file already uses `config._unwrap(node.declaration)` (see the Scenario 2 block) to peel off these wrappers before inspecting the underlying expression. The same unwrapping should be applied here:
```ts
const unwrapped =
  typeof (config as any)._unwrap === 'function'
    ? (config as any)._unwrap(node.declaration)
    : node.declaration;
return (
  t.isCallExpression(unwrapped) &&
  t.isIdentifier(unwrapped.callee) &&
  unwrapped.callee.name === methodName
);
```

The early return fires even when the required `defineMain`/`definePreview` import is absent or incomplete. Consider a file that is already structurally transformed but has no import:

```ts
export default defineMain({});
```

Here `isAlreadyTransformed` is `true` and `hasNamedExports` is `false`, so `info.source` is returned unchanged—leaving the file without its import and broken at runtime. The import-fixup block (further down the function, starting with `const configImport = …`) is never reached.

The test suite already captures this expectation (see the `'should add missing import when already transformed but import is absent'` and `'should add missing specifier when already transformed…'` tests), both of which would fail with this early return.

The guard must also verify that the correct import is present before bailing out. At minimum:
```ts
const hasCorrectImport = programNode.body.some(
  (node) =>
    t.isImportDeclaration(node) &&
    node.importKind !== 'type' &&
    node.source.value === frameworkPackage + (configType === 'main' ? '/node' : '') &&
    node.specifiers.some(
      (spec) =>
        t.isImportSpecifier(spec) &&
        t.isIdentifier(spec.imported) &&
        spec.imported.name === methodName
    )
);

if (isAlreadyTransformed && !hasNamedExports && hasCorrectImport) {
  return info.source;
}
```
